{"author":{"id":"3f8bad4585cb0f07c6570d9e31f06264af3b0abf48efbc5a44f56df5e7a9cd45"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789213422,"nonce":"qJ/Domhixm6nhb3JmKtHMMm9e4c=","title":"Linked spokes: WrenLift AOT objects linked by ash --build","message":"Per module at build time, a Wren module is loaded (source or .wlbc in the\nbundle, interpreter and JIT, reloadable even in a shipped binary) or linked\n(WrenLift's Cranelift object backend output, linked beside the Haxe objects,\nnative from the first call, full speed on JIT-less platforms).\n\nRequirements: both AOT outputs reference the core's symbols (one heap, one\nscheduler); Wren AOT roots become data-section root ranges instead of\nCranelift stack maps; a fixed symbol prefix per adapter and contribution to\nthe address-to-name table for stitched traces; bridge stubs generated at\nbuild time from the driver's type table and the Wren declaration files;\nlinked Wren on core fibers natively (no state-machine transform); plugins\nas static libraries through caribou_abi's static link path.\n\nwasm: loaded spokes only until WrenLift emits relocatable objects for ash's\nlinker. Promise the linked shape only after the WrenLift port is measured.","files":null}]}